    "prompt_texts": [
      "A compiler translates a typed mathematical program into operations that a processor can execute. The graph describes values and effects. A schedule chooses parallel work and storage. Verification checks shapes, numerical policies and buffer lifetimes before execution. Measurements distinguish compilation, transfers, kernel time and completed application calls. Explain the tradeoffs using a matrix product and a reduction. ",
      "Consider a numerical simulation of heat flowing through a metal plate. At each time step, neighboring cells exchange energy while the boundary conditions remain fixed. Describe how conservation, stability and rounding error affect the result. Write a short Python function for a finite difference update, then explain how to test it. "
    ],
